"q-569" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537961 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537961 #edb/ref 1071 "If $a={\\text{i}}^{2}$ and $b={\\text{i}}^{9}$, then $ab=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537961 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b7f8ea24-bf7b-5ebd-ac96-307434b99a43" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537961 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the addition law for exponents, we have\n\n$$\nab={\\text{i}}^{2}\\cdot {\\text{i}}^{9}={\\text{i}}^{2+9}={\\text{i}}^{11}.\n$$\n\nTo find the value of $\\text{i}$ raised to some positive integer power $n$, we divide $n$ by $4,$ and raise $\\text{i}$ to the remainder.\n\nIn our case, we have $n=11.$ Dividing the power by $4,$ we get\n\n$$\n11÷4=2\\,\\text{R}3.\n$$\n\nSo the remainder is $3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\text{i}}^{11}={\\text{i}}^{3}=-\\text{i}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537981 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537769 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537981 #edb/ref 1069 "q-86688" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537981 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537981 #edb/ref 1071 "${\\text{i}}^{-1}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537981 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e87479bf-28b6-5cab-9b25-26c4f45c1fed" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537981 #edb/ref 1074 "First, using the laws of exponents, we can write\n\n$$\n{\\text{i}}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{\\text{i}}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the numerator and denominator by $\\text{i},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\text{i}}=\\frac{1}{\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{i}}{\\text{i}}=\\frac{\\text{i}}{{\\text{i}}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now recall that ${\\text{i}}^{2}=-1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{i}}{{\\text{i}}^{2}}=\\frac{\\text{i}}{(-1)}=-\\text{i}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538012 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4298d0e8-1022-557f-ac4a-1cae4225f16c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538012 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186537981 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538016 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186538012